---

# 4. `SPL/queries.spl`

**Yahan apni actual queries paste karna.** Agar tumne dashboard banate waqt jo SPL use ki thi woh available hai, wahi use karo.

```spl
# =========================================
# Project 02 - SSH Log Analysis
# Splunk SPL Queries
# =========================================


# Total SSH Events
index=<your_index>
| stats count


# Successful SSH Login
index=<your_index>
| search <successful_login_condition>
| stats count


# Failed SSH Login
index=<your_index>
| search <failed_login_condition>
| stats count


# Failed Login by Username
index=<your_index>
| search <failed_login_condition>
| stats count by username
| sort - count


# Failed Login by Source IP
index=<your_index>
| search <failed_login_condition>
| stats count by src_ip
| sort - count


# Possible Brute Force Sources
index=<your_index>
| search <failed_login_condition>
| stats count by src_ip
| where count >= 5
| sort - count


# Source IP + Username Correlation
index=<your_index>
| search <failed_login_condition>
| stats count by src_ip username
| sort - count


# Authentication Activity Over Time
index=<your_index>
| timechart count


# Authentication Events by Status
index=<your_index>
| stats count by authentication_status
